<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Binary on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/binary/</link><description>Recent content in Binary on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 25 Nov 2012 22:03:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/binary/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Counting up to 1023</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/counting-up-to-1023/</link><pubDate>Sun, 25 Nov 2012 22:03:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/counting-up-to-1023/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Decided in the end to wire up all 10 LEDS in the LED bar graph.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Using the sketch below get the results shown in the video.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="https://ytimg.googleusercontent.com/vi/1TVgph8aZE4/0.jpg" height="266" width="320"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="https://www.youtube.com/v/1TVgph8aZE4?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="https://www.youtube.com/v/1TVgph8aZE4?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; numLed = 10;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledpins[] = {&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;13,12,11,10,9,8,7,6,5,4};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; mask[] = {&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; counter = 0;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() { &lt;br&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the digital pin as an output.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; i=0;i&amp;lt;numLed;i++){&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(ledpins[i], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(ledpins[i], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;HIGH&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;(250);&#10;  }&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Arduino Binary second counter</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-binary-second-counter/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 Nov 2012 14:46:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-binary-second-counter/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Next step with my Arduino is to set up a binary second counter.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Basic using the LED Bar Graph or six single LEDs to count seconds in binary&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjNmgs8Izk2utl30ZAVCskDyYVZ2wMyj97vYfOIO-uxLJk1cOgJ_ZaY-_LZmbyjDATFZWzCzKZQVxI7P1Y1obG7oL9eIb0x5no0MF79yfG4KTp3ruXU9Xn-ZY-ZUMVihaNaLlNvoxhBcW8/s1600/six+leds_bb.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="290" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjNmgs8Izk2utl30ZAVCskDyYVZ2wMyj97vYfOIO-uxLJk1cOgJ_ZaY-_LZmbyjDATFZWzCzKZQVxI7P1Y1obG7oL9eIb0x5no0MF79yfG4KTp3ruXU9Xn-ZY-ZUMVihaNaLlNvoxhBcW8/s320/six+leds_bb.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;/*&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;Binary&amp;nbsp;Second&amp;nbsp;Counter&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Created&amp;nbsp;Alastair&amp;nbsp;Montgomery&amp;nbsp;22/11/2012&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*/&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledPins[] = {&#10;  7,8,9,10,11,12};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; mask[] = {&#10;  1,2,4,8,16,32};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledCount = 6;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() {&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; thisPin =0; thisPin &amp;lt; ledCount; thisPin++) {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(ledPins[thisPin], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sanity Checking my new Arduino Uno Board</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sanity-checking-my-new-arduino-uno-board/</link><pubDate>Thu, 22 Nov 2012 22:13:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sanity-checking-my-new-arduino-uno-board/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Quick sanity check of my new Arduino board using a LED Bar Graph.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object width="320" height="266" class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="https://ytimg.googleusercontent.com/vi/L7ri5PBrsQU/0.jpg"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="https://www.youtube.com/v/L7ri5PBrsQU?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="https://www.youtube.com/v/L7ri5PBrsQU?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Here is the sketch I will be using.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; led1 = 8;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; led2 = 9;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; counter = 0;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() { &lt;br&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the digital pin as an output.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(led2, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&lt;br&gt;&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;loop&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() {&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (counter &amp;amp; 1) {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;HIGH&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;LOW&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>